```go
func (index *Index) scanPageLocked(from, to int64, filter txFilter, window timeWindow, order TxOrder, offset int64, pageSize int) (hits []TxHit, total, blocks int64)
```

I'll add a `qualified map[string]struct{}` param; nil means accept all. When non-nil, occurrence survives only if tx in qualified.

And a new function:

```go
// qualifyingIDsLocked counts, for every identifier passing filter, the
// distinct in-range blocks (also passing window) holding it, and returns the
// set of identifiers reaching minBlocks. The caller must hold index.mu.
func (index *Index) qualifyingIDsLocked(from, to int64, filter txFilter, window timeWindow, minBlocks int64) map[string]struct{}
```

Implementation: map[string]map[int64]struct{}? That could be memory-heavy. Better: map[string]int64 count plus map[string]int64 lastBlock? No — same id can appear in non-consecutive blocks; counting distinct blocks needs per-id last-seen block only if we process blocks in order and dedupe within a block. Trick: iterate blocks in increasing height; for each block, collect the set of distinct matching ids in that block; for each, increment count[id]. That's O(distinct ids per block) memory — fine. Since we process each block once and dedupe within the block, distinct-block counting is exact.

```go
func (index *Index) qualifyingIDsLocked(from, to int64, filter txFilter, window timeWindow, minBlocks int64) map[string]struct{} {
    counts := make(map[string]int64)
    for height := from; height <= to; height++ {
        block := index.Blocks[height]
        if !window.contains(block.Time) {
            continue
        }
        seen := make(map[string]struct{}, len(block.Txs))
        for _, tx := range block.Txs {
            if !filter.matches(tx) {
                continue
            }
            if _, ok := seen[tx]; ok {
                continue
            }
            seen[tx] = struct{}{}
            counts[tx]++
        }
    }
    qualified := make(map[string]struct{}, len(counts))
    for id, n := range counts {
        if n >= minBlocks {
            qualified[id] = struct{}{}
        }
    }
    return qualified
}
```

